  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759918,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 16t: A Bug-Squashing Adventure for Sega Genesis\n\nStep into the digital world of 16t, a unique 1991 action game for the Sega Genesis, originally released on the Sega Game Toshokan service. You assume the role of a computer programmer tasked with debugging a malfunctioning program – literally!  Enter a bizarre, pixelated landscape where levels are looping platforms, and your weapon of choice is a colossal 16-ton weight.\n\nGameplay revolves around strategically tossing these massive weights to crush the digital \"bugs\" that infest the program.  Use the A and C buttons to jump and the B button to launch your weighty projectiles.  A limited number of weights can be held at once, displayed at the bottom of the screen, requiring careful planning and timing.  Be wary, however! A single hit or being crushed yourself results in a lost life.\n\nOriginally released via Sega's Meganet service in Japan, 16t later found its way onto the Sega CD as part of the *Game no Kanzume Vol. 2* compilation.  Master the bounce and trajectory of your weights, as even they can rebound and crush you if mishandled!"
    },
